title:: CaosSequencer
summary:: Owner of time: index, BPM, stepDur, randomTime and playhead.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosTrack, Classes/CaosBox

description::
The sequencer owns the 0..size-1 index, the step duration in beats, the BPM and
the random-time mode. The GUI and the API talk to it; tracks receive only their
step.

instancemethods::

method:: play
method:: pause
method:: stop
code::play:: starts or resumes; code::pause:: keeps the step; code::stop:: returns
to 0.

method:: bpm
method:: stepDur
method:: randomTime
method:: externalClock
code::
s = CaosSequencer.new(step: {|i| i.postln }, size: 32);
s.bpm = 126;
s.stepDur = 0.25;
s.randomTime = true;
s.externalClock = true; // the tempo comes from a slave clock
::
With code::externalClock:: true, code::bpm:: and code::onTempoChange:: keep
working, but the sequencer does not write code::TempoClock.tempo::. The slave
sync owns the tempo; code::randomTime:: is ignored while the flag is on.

method:: onTempoChange
Callback code::{|bpm| ... }:: when the effective tempo changes, including the value
chosen in random time.

method:: onLoop
Callback code::{|sequencer| ... }:: after the last step of a full loop, when the
index wraps to 0. Used by code::CaosBox.randPattern::; it avoids a second clock or
an external Tdef.
